  "articleBody": "Deciding between wall sconces and recessed lights for your stairway can feel like a tough choice, but each has its perks depending on your home's needs and your personal style. Wall sconces, for example, can add a decorative touch and provide a softer, more diffused light, often great for wider stairways where they won't feel obtrusive. Recessed lights, on the other hand, offer a cleaner, more minimalist look, tucking discreetly into the wall or ceiling to provide targeted illumination without any visual clutter. They're often a fantastic choice for narrower stairways where space is at a premium and you want to avoid anything that projects too far. When you're making your choice, think about glare control, how easy the fixtures will be to maintain, and what kind of rating you need if your stairway is in an area with a lot of moisture. Most importantly, ensure the fixture output is strong enough to light up the treads and landings, reaching at least 1 foot-candle at the center, as recommended. If you're struggling to decide or worried about meeting code, don't hesitate to reach out to a professional who can help you weigh your options and plan the ideal setup.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
